<title>BRAZIL: Brazil bolsas halt trade in Petrobras.</title>
<headline>Brazil bolsas halt trade in Petrobras.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian stock exchanges said they would suspend Thursday trade in state oil firm Petrobras following a request by the Securities and Exchange Commission (CVM).  </p>
<p>Brazil's CVM requested the suspension until Petrobras determines a course of action after a Rio de Janeiro court issued a sentence ordering the company to pay 3.406 billion reais ($3.25 billion) to Petroquisa's minority shareholders.</p>
<p>Petroquisa is a Petrobras holding company responsible for petrochemical production. Most of the company's subsidiaries were sold off during the first phase of Brazil's privatisation program between 1992 and 1995.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom +5511 248</p>
